WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.030
- Hi, it's Rie.

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:03.010
Today, a friend will be challenging me

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:06.480
to take a popular food and Make It Fancy.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.280
Today's guest is Andrew!

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.430
- Rie, I wanna challenge
you to make eggnog fancy.

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:14.720
In the winter, a warm cup of eggnog

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.070
is one of the best things to have.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.020
I've always wondered what are other ways

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.980
that I could enjoy this drink.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.830
So I wanna see you make eggnog fancy

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.040
and see what you come up with.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:24.930
- Eggnog.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.130
I've never had eggnog before.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:29.090
Very controversial drink.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:32.250
It seems like this one is non-alcoholic,

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:35.030
but typically served with alcohol.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.467
It's yellow.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:39.670
(playful music)

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:40.830
Oh, it's very sweet.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:44.470
Milkshake almost, but with egg.

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:46.407
I prefer milkshake.

00:00:46.407 --> 00:00:48.040
(Producer and Rie laugh)

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.610
It's so creamy.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:52.060
The spice definitely have a

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.830
like holiday Christmas feeling to it.

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:56.750
I think flavor-wise it's good.

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:00.260
It's just, I don't wanna
drink this (laughs).

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.430
I've got some great idea

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:04.232
and I'm excited to Make It Fancy.

00:01:04.232 --> 00:01:06.610
(playful music)

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:08.240
All right, here's what I got.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:11.920
Heavy cream, butter, cream cheese, eggs.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.600
From the pantry, I got flour, brown sugar,

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.340
meringue powder, gelatin
powder, condensed milk,

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:22.769
salt, vanilla extract, nutmeg, allspice,

00:01:22.769 --> 00:01:26.830
cinnamon, powdered sugar,
lemon, baking powder,

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:31.010
sprinkles, food coloring and spiced rum.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:33.290
All right, let's get started.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:34.563
Make It Fancy.

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:40.700
So first, our room temperature butter.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.880
I have two stick and a half.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:45.210
One cup of brown sugar.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:48.130
Mix them together using stand mixer.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:51.200
I'm going to mix until light and fluffy

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.060
and color is a little bit lighter.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.080
Add egg yolk one by one.

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:59.680
Make sure each yolk's well incorporated

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.470
and scrape the side.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.990
Okay, so all the eggs are incorporated

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:07.050
so I'm going to add quarter cup of eggnog.

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:08.680
If you don't have stand mixer,

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.620
you can use hand mixer
or you can use whisk,

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:12.960
but it will take longer.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.390
We are using spiced rum.

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:17.270
I think it's gonna be a nice additional

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.060
adult holiday flavor.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:21.870
And I'm adding one tablespoon.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:25.221
- [Producer] George Washington
had his own eggnog recipe.

00:02:25.221 --> 00:02:26.054
- Ooh!

00:02:26.054 --> 00:02:30.820
- [Producer] And it had rye
whiskey, rum and sherry.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.620
- He's the original triple alcohol.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.730
Yeah, back then, they
didn't have internet,

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.560
but they had alcohol.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.540
I'm going to make my flour mixture.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:43.300
Pinch of allspice.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.090
Half teaspoon of cinnamon.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:47.130
Quarter teaspoon of salt.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:49.380
One teaspoon of baking powder.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.863
Grate nutmeg, about half a teaspoon.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:55.820
Grated my finger.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.970
And lightly mix.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:00.296
I'm gonna add half.

00:03:00.296 --> 00:03:02.450
(mixer whirs)

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:04.030
Rest of that.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:05.730
You want to mix until

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:08.060
you won't see any visible flour bits.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:11.440
Transfer this dough into a plastic.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:14.720
Wrap it tight and rest this
dough in a refrigerator

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:16.230
about two hours.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:18.125
Two hours later.

00:03:18.125 --> 00:03:19.103
Remove plastic.

00:03:20.123 --> 00:03:23.780
From this dough, I'm going
to measure 10 ounces.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.740
Between two parchment paper,

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:28.440
I'm adding dough and start rolling.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:33.040
Still cold so it's a
little bit tough to roll,

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.510
but gradually soften up.

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:40.440
So you want to roll out about
one-eighth inch thickness

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.320
and about 11-inch diameter

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.610
and I'm going to line this dough.

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:50.510
Use your finger, line into the tart mold.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:54.840
Using rolling pin and
roll over couple times

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:58.040
and it will naturally fold like a magic.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.250
We are going to dock this dough.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:02.470
So when you dock this, it doesn't puffs up

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.120
and it doesn't shrink.

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:07.210
I'm going to put this in
the freezer for 20 minutes.

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:09.500
Bake at 450 for five minutes,

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:12.500
then lower the temperature to 350

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.730
and bake another 15 minutes.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.630
I have rest of the dough right here

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:19.130
and I'm going to roll same way.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.550
This dough is still a little bit tough

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:23.790
so you can kind of tap it

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:26.640
and make it easier to roll.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:29.070
Just take off the top parchment paper.

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:31.360
I'm using star-shaped cookie cutter

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:33.390
and dust with flour.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:35.730
Making star-shaped cookie

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:38.990
and you're gonna line
in your parchment paper.

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:43.660
You kinda wanna push
from behind and mold it.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:48.330
I'm going to unmold this
and bake 350 for 10 minutes.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.060
Quarter cup of eggnog,

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.280
quarter cup of heavy cream,

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:54.430
quarter cup of brown sugar,

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:56.730
one tablespoon of butter.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:59.400
Mix it until well combined.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:00.540
Bring it to a boil

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:02.470
and cook about five minutes.

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:03.730
Mix occasionally.

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:05.200
- [Producer] Back in the 1800s,

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.710
eggnog was used to treat diseases.

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:09.630
- Was there alcohol in it?

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:11.280
I cook about five minutes

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.970
and it's kind of bubbly
and it look thicker

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:17.360
and I'm gonna start whisking
constantly from this point

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:20.230
'cause you don't want mixture to be burnt

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:23.540
and I'm going to cook
about two more minutes.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:24.560
It smells good.

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:25.590
This looks done.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:26.660
It's very thick.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:30.750
Pour this into a heat-safe glass bowl.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:34.170
Set this aside to cool in room temperature

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:35.780
and moving on to the next step.

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:37.810
One tablespoon of water

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:42.640
and sprinkle one and
half teaspoon of gelatin.

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:44.680
Let it bloom about five minutes.

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:47.140
While I'm waiting, mix cream cheese

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:50.830
with hand mixer until fluffy.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:53.880
Seven ounces of condensed milk

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.000
and once it's well mixed,

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.013
add in half cup of eggnog,

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:02.794
one tablespoon of lemon juice.

00:06:02.794 --> 00:06:05.399
(hand mixer whirs)

00:06:05.399 --> 00:06:09.170
then adding half teaspoon
of vanilla extract,

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:12.180
quarter teaspoon of cinnamon powder,

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:15.790
about one-eighth teaspoon of nutmeg.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.085
Blend well.

00:06:17.085 --> 00:06:19.930
(hand mixer whirs)

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:24.420
One tablespoon of hot
water to bloom the gelatin.

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:27.550
Make sure it's all melted in hot water.

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:30.953
Gelatin into the mixture and mix well.

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:36.040
Strain this mixture so I can
make sure this is smooth.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.730
Okay, mixture is ready but
I have more things to do.

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:42.220
My tart shell is baked and cool,

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:45.370
and I transfer my mixture into pitcher

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:47.070
so I can easily pour.

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:50.110
And this is the eggnog
butterscotch I made.

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:52.180
Pour this mixture.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:54.710
You don't want to overfill it.

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:58.340
Give a nice drop of butterscotch.

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:01.990
Using skewers and kind
of makes nice pattern.

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:03.460
Just a freeform.

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:05.700
Pattern looks pretty and
I'm going to chill this

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:08.300
in a refrigerator about six hours.

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:10.120
Four cup of powdered sugar,

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:14.020
quarter cup of meringue
powder, and mix well.

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:14.853
Add water.

00:07:14.853 --> 00:07:17.520
Start with four tablespoon first

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:22.310
and adding more water
until desired consistency.

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:24.580
So I added meringue powder.

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.460
It's faster to set if you add it,

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:28.060
but if you don't have meringue powder,

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:31.870
you can just add egg whites
or corn syrup and water,

00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:34.330
but it will take longer to set.

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:36.400
This is a good consistency.

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:38.700
It's ready like this because
I'm going to pipe it.

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:42.120
Divide into three bowls

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:46.150
and I'm adding one with
green food coloring

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:47.860
and this one is red.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:51.590
I'm gonna add this to a piping bag.

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:53.760
Green, white.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:57.010
My eggnog cookies are baked and cooled.

00:07:57.010 --> 00:08:01.200
Now I'm going to decorate
with icing and sprinkles.

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:03.510
It's just a freestyle.

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:05.950
You want to kinda draw the outline

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:08.440
and kinda fill the space.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.410
And while it's still wet,

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:15.410
I'm gonna just put some
red and white sprinkles.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:19.310
So it's kind of cool if
you put like big sprinkles.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.220
Kind of look like Rudolph.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:23.120
Put the green sprinkle.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:26.040
So this one I'm going to decorate,

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:27.630
look like a snowflake.

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:30.110
This is probably my favorite pattern.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:33.060
Okay, holiday cookies looks very festive

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:34.570
but we are not done yet.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:36.070
A cup of heavy cream,

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:38.250
two tablespoon of eggnog,

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:41.220
quarter cup of powdered sugar,

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.570
half teaspoon of nutmeg.

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:45.930
I'm gonna use immersion blender.

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:48.652
Mix it until stiff thick.

00:08:48.652 --> 00:08:51.550
Spiced rum, one tablespoon.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:55.260
I usually use whisk but I
think this is a cool trick.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:58.720
Transfer this into a piping bag.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:00.480
We're gonna use it later.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:03.752
This is the tart I was
resting in the refrigerator.

00:09:03.752 --> 00:09:06.920
It's set now and I'm going to decorate.

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:10.610
Using star tip and piping straight.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:12.170
If you want to make bigger star,

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:15.710
just press and hold it and make it bigger,

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:17.880
and if you want to make it smaller stars,

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:20.260
you can just lightly squeeze.

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:25.260
I'm placing bigger cookies first
and small cookies around it

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:28.430
so it kinda look like a Milky Way

00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:33.400
and filling with eggnog cream in the gap.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:35.383
And we are done!

00:09:36.567 --> 00:09:39.650
(light string music)

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:46.590
Holiday eggnog tart.

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:47.433
Very festive!

00:09:48.761 --> 00:09:51.020
(cheerful music)

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:53.420
I have a Christmas gift for you.

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:54.253
- Really.

00:09:54.253 --> 00:09:55.086
- Yeah.

00:09:55.086 --> 00:09:55.919
- Oh, a hat.

00:09:55.919 --> 00:09:57.460
I was like, it's this cake, right.

00:09:57.460 --> 00:09:59.043
Thank you.
- A fancy cap.

00:10:00.304 --> 00:10:01.720
- He has a big head.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:04.990
- Made eggnog fancy as
you challenged me and--

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:06.150
- This does look so fancy.

00:10:06.150 --> 00:10:07.550
Is that what this is, butterscotch,

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:09.110
this little flower design?

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:10.700
That's the kind of
thing where I look at it

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:12.860
and I'm like, I will never make desserts

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:14.210
as well as whoever made this.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:15.230
Is this a face?

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:16.470
Is this like a person?

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:20.360
- It was inspired by Rudolph.

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:22.080
- So is there booze in this tart?

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:24.050
- Yes, always.

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:25.120
- I mean, look at that!

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:27.260
- You always have a very particular way

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:28.340
of inspecting (laughs).

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:32.300
- I like to get it onto my same elevation

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:35.330
and I also like to really smell something.

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:36.667
- Cheers
- Cheers.

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:38.980
This is a treat.

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:39.813
- Thank you.

00:10:39.813 --> 00:10:42.400
- This is like what I
dream of when I think of

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:44.570
a holiday treat.

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:47.930
- All right, Andrew, do you
remember what we do after?

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:50.631
- Yeah, you do like some
John Travolta disco.

00:10:50.631 --> 00:10:52.162
(Rie laughs)

00:10:52.162 --> 00:10:54.415
- [Producer] He had his
own version, actually.

00:10:54.415 --> 00:10:55.560
- Did I?

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:56.400
- You are John Travolta.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:58.126
Three, two, one.

00:10:58.126 --> 00:11:00.504
Make It Fancy.
- Make it Fancy.

00:11:00.504 --> 00:11:03.254
(cheerful music)

